{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_w56ynyff2skceb7szkzrfw3h7inw4bcjwwrjbafiuviz6kvcq7aa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01WvKbUkYhs7DYepKfBgc5Pn","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/harvest-work-pCkDmR/translated_rust/build.rs","old_string":"// Build script that mirrors the C library's exported symbol set.\n//\n// `cc` (and the GNU linker) emits `_init` / `_fini` from crti.o/crtn.o into\n// every shared library, but Rust's default version script hides them. The C\n// build does not apply such a version script, so those symbols stay public.\n// To keep the dynamic-symbol table identical to the C build, we tell the\n// linker to dynamically export `_init` and `_fini` from the Rust cdylib.\nfn main() {\n    println!(\"cargo:rustc-link-arg=-Wl,--export-dynamic-symbol=_init\");\n    println!(\"cargo:rustc-link-arg=-Wl,--export-dynamic-symbol=_fini\");\n}","new_string":"// Build script that mirrors the C library's exported symbol set.\n//\n// `cc` (and the GNU linker) emits `_init` / `_fini` from crti.o/crtn.o into\n// every shared library, but Rust's default `--version-script` confines the\n// dynamic-symbol table to the symbols Rust itself exports, hiding `_init`\n// and `_fini`. The C build does not apply such a version script, so those\n// symbols stay public.\n//\n// To keep the dynamic-symbol table identical to the C build, we instruct\n// `rustc` to allow multiple definitions and we provide our own (empty)\n// `_init` and `_fini` functions in lib.rs marked `#[no_mangle]`. With\n// `-z muldefs`, our definitions are emitted into the dynamic symbol table\n// while the duplicate copies from crti.o / crtn.o are silently discarded.\nfn main() {\n    println!(\"cargo:rustc-link-arg=-Wl,-z,muldefs\");\n}"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":334,"cache_read_input_tokens":46258,"ca